{
  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case02",
  "description": "THE TRUNCATION CASE, and the sharpest expectation in this gate. COMPUTE WS-MONTHLY-INT = ( TRAN-CAT-BAL * DIS-INT-RATE) / 1200 at :464-465 carries NO ROUNDED phrase - the keyword occurs zero times in all twenty-eight programs - so the store into WS-MONTHLY-INT PIC S9(09)V99 at :168 truncates. 1000.00 at 12.50 has an exact product of 12500.0000 and an exact quotient of 10.41666..., whose third decimal digit is six: that is the only kind of operand pair that can tell truncation from rounding. TRAN-AMT therefore carries 0000000104A - the zoned image of 10.41 with the sign overpunched onto its trailing byte - and NOT 0000000104B, which is 10.42 and is what this system would write if it rounded. The ACCOUNT IS acctdata.txt ROW 0 VERBATIM, ACCT-GROUP-ID and all, so the arithmetic is proven against a real production account row: its group is ten spaces, the READ at :416 misses, :418-419 display, and the retry at :437-438 finds the rate under 'DEFAULT   '. Only the disclosure-group row is stated inline, because no row of discgrp.txt carries 12.50 and no row of tcatbal.txt carries a non-zero balance - the category-balance row is written in that fixture's own 50-byte shape, FILLER span of zeros included.",
